//! check: fail(E0301)
//! phase: parse
//! conforms: mod.dir, gram.item.use, conf.resolve.ambient
//!
//! wolf-lang#1083: the package has a module `worker` (the directory beside
//! this file), and this file calls it with no `use worker`. `worker` is
//! also one of the prelude's provisional stand-ins, so until this row the
//! name resolved to the stand-in and every compiled tier declined it as "a
//! std/prelude stub without a signature", a refusal that blamed the
//! compiler. An unimported module of a stand-in's name now misses as every
//! unimported module does, E0301 at the name, with a note that the module
//! is not imported and `use worker` as the edit. `module_unimported/` is
//! the same program with the module named `helper`.

fn main() -> int {
    let args = env_args()
    return worker.main(args) // ERROR E0301: add `use worker`
}
